- Daemon-local dependencies: `internal/analysis/diagnostics`, `internal/analysis/netintel`, `internal/analysis/peerdiscovery`, `internal/analysis/provider`, `internal/analysis/scanner`, `internal/foundation/capabilities`, `internal/foundation/config`, `internal/foundation/flowregistry`, `internal/foundation/pingcache`, `internal/foundation/redact`, `internal/foundation/remoteaction`, `internal/foundation/store`, `internal/foundation/trafficstats`, `internal/foundation/updateadmission`, `internal/integrations/captchaclient`, `internal/integrations/presets`, `internal/integrations/provision`, `internal/integrations/sub`, `internal/integrations/vpngate`, `internal/native/bridge`, `internal/networking/dns`, `internal/networking/dnstunnel`, `internal/networking/geoip`, `internal/networking/kcppolicy`, `internal/networking/proxyconfig`, `internal/networking/routing`, `internal/platform/process`, `internal/platform/system`, `internal/protocols/tarpit`, `internal/runtime/proxy`, `internal/runtime/routingplugin`, `internal/runtime/runtimecore`, `internal/runtime/safety`, `internal/runtime/trust`, `internal/runtime/warp`, `internal/workflows/jobs`.
- Direct daemon callers: `cmd`.
- External/shared imports: 1 distinct package(s); inspect source before changing dependency contracts.

## Invariants
- Gin registration plus GET /api/routes is served-route truth.
- Request-scoped work propagates request context; handlers do not create daemon lifetime.
- Disconnected/simulated features fail closed instead of reporting operational success.
- `adapters` code must not import a higher-rank daemon band.

